                <pb facs="0603" n="593" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg593"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">638.5131/182: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Finley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-16T09:00:00-05:00">October 16, 1937—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>91. Haitian Government has just informed me that on October 11 it instructed
                    Chatelain to advise the Quai D’Orsay that Haiti would be willing to conclude the
                    proposed commercial convention with France if it can be granted a quota of
                    100,000 instead of 120,000 quintals of coffee.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Finley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
